\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Class Description \

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 An NSSliderCell controls the appearance and behavior of an NSSlider, or of a single slider in an NSMatrix.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 You can customize an NSSliderCell to a certain degree, using its 
\b set...
\b0  methods. If these do not allow you sufficient flexibility, you can create a subclass. In that subclass, you can override any of the following methods:
\b  knobRectFlipped:
\b0 , 
\b drawBarInside:flipped:
\b0 , 
\b drawKnob:
\b0 , or 
\b prefersTrackingUntilMouseUp
\b0 .\

\fs14 \

